.he "dd (1)                       8/16/26                       dd (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
dd
- convert and copy a file
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
dd [ option=value ... ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Dd copies the standard input to the standard output, converting on the
way if it is asked to, unless if= or of= points it at files.  The
block sizes may be set to suit raw devices.
.sp
A size argument is a number, which may end in k, b or w to multiply by
1024, 512 or 2, and two numbers may be multiplied by putting x between
them.  After the copy, dd reports the number of whole and partial
records read and written.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
OPTIONS
.in +5
.br
.in +10
.ti -10
if=file	Read from file rather than the standard input.

.ti -10
of=file	Write to file rather than the standard output.

.ti -10
ibs=n	Read in blocks of n bytes; the default is 512.

.ti -10
obs=n	Write in blocks of n bytes; the default is 512.

.ti -10
bs=n	Set both input and output block size to n, superseding ibs and obs.  With no conversion this also skips the copy from the input buffer to the output buffer.

.ti -10
cbs=n	Set the conversion buffer size, used by the ascii, ebcdic, ibm, block and unblock conversions.

.ti -10
skip=n	Skip n input records before copying.

.ti -10
seek=n	Seek n records into the output file before copying.

.ti -10
count=n	Copy only n input records.

.ti -10
files=n	Copy n input files before stopping; useful only on a device such as a tape.

.ti -10
conv=ascii	Convert EBCDIC to ASCII.

.ti -10
conv=ebcdic	Convert ASCII to EBCDIC.

.ti -10
conv=ibm	A slightly different map of ASCII to EBCDIC.

.ti -10
conv=block	Convert variable length records to fixed length, padding with blanks to cbs.

.ti -10
conv=unblock	Convert fixed length records to variable length, trimming trailing blanks and adding a newline.

.ti -10
conv=lcase	Map upper case to lower case.

.ti -10
conv=ucase	Map lower case to upper case.

.ti -10
conv=swab	Swap each pair of bytes.

.ti -10
conv=noerror	Do not stop on a read error.

.ti -10
conv=sync	Pad every input record to ibs.

.in -10
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
Several conversions may be given after conv=, separated by commas.  Of
ascii, ebcdic, ibm, block and unblock only the last named is used.
When copying a raw disk with bad sectors, conv=noerror,sync keeps dd
in step.
.sp
The port made the record counts long, so a copy is no longer cut off
at 32k records as it was on the PDP-11; block sizes, however, are
still capped at 32000 bytes, and a larger one is refused.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
cp (1)
